    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "For his capstone project, Tanner Christensen choreographed and recorded a dance performance that centered on both the historical and contemporary aspects of queerness as a human rights concept. His accompanying research paper delves into the intricacies of his artwork and the literature that influence it. From dance literature about the Alvin Ailey Dance Company to a podcast on the employment of lobotomies on gay men in the 20th century, his research informed the choreography of his performance and the analysis presented in his paper. He ultimately decided to do a performance piece for his capstone to break the logic that scholarship typically affords. Through this medium, Tanner was able to portray the intersection of identity, history, and circumstance visually and emotionally from a human rights standpoint.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Christensen, T. (2024). Take a Breath: A Dance Exploration Investigating LGBTQ+ Rights. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/ch294ch7245. https://doi.org/10.25740/ch294ch7245.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
